sequenceDiagram
    actor "User" as User
    actor "Mobile Client (Flutter)" as MobileClientFlutter
    participant "API Host (ASP.NET Core)" as APIHostASPNETCore
    actor "Users Module" as UsersModule
    participant "Deletion Job Queue" as DeletionJobQueue
    participant "Deletion Worker" as DeletionWorker
    participant "Primary Database" as PrimaryDatabase
    participant "Log Anonymization Service" as LogAnonymizationService
    participant "Application Logs" as ApplicationLogs
    participant "Immutable Audit Trail" as ImmutableAuditTrail

    activate MobileClientFlutter
    User->>MobileClientFlutter: 1. 1. Confirms irreversible account deletion via UI dialog
    activate APIHostASPNETCore
    MobileClientFlutter->>APIHostASPNETCore: 2. 2. DELETE /api/v1/users/me
    APIHostASPNETCore-->>MobileClientFlutter: HTTP 202 Accepted
    activate UsersModule
    APIHostASPNETCore->>UsersModule: 3. 3. InitiateAccountDeletion(userId)
    UsersModule-->>APIHostASPNETCore: JobQueuedSuccessfully
    UsersModule->>ImmutableAuditTrail: 4. 4. CreateAuditLog(event: ACCOUNT_DELETION_REQUEST)
    UsersModule->>DeletionJobQueue: 5. 5. SendMessage(payload)
    UsersModule->>UsersModule: 6. 6. InvalidateUserSession()
    MobileClientFlutter->>MobileClientFlutter: 7. 7. Clear local session & navigate to login
    activate DeletionWorker
    DeletionJobQueue->>DeletionWorker: 8. 8. [Async] Polls and receives deletion message
    DeletionWorker->>PrimaryDatabase: 9. 9. DELETE FROM Users WHERE UserId = @userId; (Cascading Deletes)
    PrimaryDatabase-->>DeletionWorker: Rows Affected
    activate LogAnonymizationService
    DeletionWorker->>LogAnonymizationService: 10. 10. TriggerAnonymization(userId, ipAddress)
    LogAnonymizationService->>ApplicationLogs: 11. 11. Search and update log entries containing PII
    ApplicationLogs-->>LogAnonymizationService: Anonymization Complete
    DeletionWorker->>ImmutableAuditTrail: 12. 12. CreateAuditLog(event: ACCOUNT_DELETION_COMPLETE)
    DeletionWorker->>DeletionJobQueue: 13. 13. DeleteMessage()

    note over ImmutableAuditTrail: The Audit Trail (LOG-AUDIT-TRAIL) must be configured with immutability features like Amazon S3 Ob...
    note over DeletionWorker: The Deletion Worker must be idempotent to handle potential retries from SQS without causing error...
    note over DeletionJobQueue: A CloudWatch Alarm must be configured on the SQS Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) to immediately notify th...

    deactivate LogAnonymizationService
    deactivate DeletionWorker
    deactivate UsersModule
    deactivate APIHostASPNETCore
    deactivate MobileClientFlutter
